WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.900
RL training is driving models to abandon English and chain-of-thought traces, revealing internal reasoning that no longer needs human language. Builders who verify or audit those traces now need inspection methods that do not assume the intermediate steps stay readable. This is Models &amp; Agents, Episode 210, calibrated unlearning and clinical quantization land next, then latent agent memory and multilingual web agents, then things to try and on the horizon. Andre Carpathi wrote on X

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:35.200
that current reinforcement learning post-training is working, measured by traces that stay coherent.

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:40.340
He pointed to internal representations that are more efficient for the task than natural language.

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:46.500
That matches earlier reports of models inventing private token sequences during long horizon tasks.

00:00:47.748 --> 00:00:53.388
H2DF arrives on archive as calibrated target bands for controllable language model unlearning.

00:00:53.988 --> 00:00:57.828
Unbounded gradient ascent is replaced by a data dependent target band.

00:00:57.828 --> 00:01:02.888
pressure applies only below a lower threshold and reverses once that band is reached.

00:01:03.428 --> 00:01:08.588
Each step uses one forget batch pass, with sparse retain replay every tenth step.

00:01:09.148 --> 00:01:14.248
On Tofu, the method matches grad diff forget and retain negative log likelihood, while

00:01:14.248 --> 00:01:15.088
cutting variability.

00:01:15.788 --> 00:01:19.688
On Muse News, retention improves over gradient ascent and NPO.

00:01:20.776 --> 00:01:26.336
Accented English automatic speech recognition, or ASR, is the target of mixture of phonetic

00:01:26.336 --> 00:01:33.256
experts low-rank adaptation or Laura for conformer models. The archive method places six low-rank

00:01:33.256 --> 00:01:38.976
experts aligned to manner of articulation classes. Routing happens at the frame level with a hybrid

00:01:38.976 --> 00:01:44.596
phoneme plus acoustic gate. The shared expert set removes the need for accent-specific modules

00:01:44.596 --> 00:01:52.776
and supports zero-shot transfer to held out accents. On L2ARCTIC, it delivers a 12.3% relative word

00:01:52.776 --> 00:01:56.776
error rate improvement over single-lora in the zero-shot setting.

00:01:57.660 --> 00:02:02.020
Clinical verification decisions get a statistical certificate from CERTA.

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:07.640
The archive work decides when an 8-bit or 4-bit quantized model can safely replace its

00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:10.400
BF-16 reference for a given clinical decision.

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:16.100
Across 11 models, the 8-bit path covered 99.8-100% of decisions.

00:02:16.760 --> 00:02:22.920
The 4-bit frontier cut amortized costs to roughly 26% of the BF-16 baseline, while

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:29.550
While staying under 48 GB, multi-hop rag and Casper MP are the test beds for evidence-based

00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:36.010
generation with retrieval augmented generation, or rag, EBG on archive requires line-level

00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:38.850
citations and scores both correctness and grounding.

00:02:39.830 --> 00:02:44.470
Similarity retrieval reliably surfaces any relevant chunk, but frequently misses the full

00:02:44.470 --> 00:02:46.530
set needed for multi-fact questions.

00:02:47.190 --> 00:02:51.210
Chunking erase's document level metadata required for identity resolution.

00:02:51.210 --> 00:02:57.564
Culture Lens varies country, value, true norm, and contradictory norm evidence in an archive

00:02:57.564 --> 00:03:05.024
study of cultural reasoning. The suite runs 9,261 scenarios. Stating a contradictory norm

00:03:05.024 --> 00:03:11.144
drops aligned answers by 32 to 47 points, even when the model knows the correct country norm.

00:03:11.784 --> 00:03:16.464
Blocking the contradictory norm inside the model restores the correct answer in most cases.

00:03:16.464 --> 00:03:24.804
Supervised fine-tuning on contradictory norm examples raises align performance to 85% to 93% on unseen countries.

00:03:25.750 --> 00:03:32.370
Inserting a learned readout token and training a confidence probe on its hidden state is the method in a new archive paper.

00:03:32.950 --> 00:03:39.130
The approach outperforms probes that read from existing vocabulary tokens on multiple data sets and model families.

00:03:39.730 --> 00:03:42.650
Extending it to multiple learned tokens yields further gains.

00:03:42.650 --> 00:03:46.350
The change is a drop-in replacement for any existing probe.

00:03:47.349 --> 00:03:52.389
ALF World is one test bed where LAMM keeps competing hypotheses without emitting text.

00:03:52.889 --> 00:03:59.909
The archive agent encodes interaction evidence in a shared common state and competing hypotheses in weighted delta components.

00:04:00.529 --> 00:04:04.529
Updates run recurrently from action outcome predictions without emitting text.

00:04:04.989 --> 00:04:11.869
On ALF World, it raises success rate at 30 by 6 points and cuts redundant actions by 17.7 points.

00:04:11.869 --> 00:04:18.177
science. On Science World's success rises 22 points. Hindi, Bengali, Urdu, and

00:04:18.177 --> 00:04:23.197
Amharic join English on six fully localized websites in low agent. The archive

00:04:23.197 --> 00:04:28.477
benchmark yields 3,000 task instances. Both closed and open source agents drop

00:04:28.477 --> 00:04:32.597
sharply on the low resource languages, with open source models showing the

00:04:32.597 --> 00:04:36.877
largest degradation. Post-training on a small subset of traces recover

00:04:36.877 --> 00:04:42.576
substantial performance. Group relative credit assignment is how GRSE decides which

00:04:42.576 --> 00:04:43.996
agent's skill should change.

00:04:44.496 --> 00:04:49.856
The archive method runs each question multiple times under the same skill libraries and contrasts

00:04:49.856 --> 00:04:53.116
executions to assign credit to specific agent's skill pairs.

00:04:53.796 --> 00:04:57.996
On hotpot QA, it outperforms MA skills on multi-hop questions.

00:04:58.436 --> 00:05:03.336
On corrupted libraries, it correctly signs every planted harmful skill and recovers clean

00:05:03.336 --> 00:05:04.436
library performance.

00:05:05.457 --> 00:05:09.837
Multimodal medical workflows get a vision language planner in MED agent plus.

00:05:09.837 --> 00:05:14.997
the archive system pairs that planner with 18 specialist models spanning 12 tasks

00:05:14.997 --> 00:05:16.277
and 8 modalities.

00:05:16.657 --> 00:05:21.657
The planner achieves 91% tool-call accuracy in single-tool multi-round settings.

00:05:22.507 --> 00:05:26.177
Accuracy is 80.7% in multi-tool single-round settings.

00:05:26.577 --> 00:05:32.217
End-to-end accuracy on held-out cases reaches 0.98, matching dedicated specialists.

00:05:33.345 --> 00:05:37.225
Simon Willisn published the exact prompt he uses for AI proofreading.

00:05:37.225 --> 00:05:43.825
he placed it in his agentic engineering patterns guide on his site. Simon Willison, after an audio-only

00:05:43.825 --> 00:05:49.805
multiplayer mode caused motion sickness, added a web-socket relay for real online multiplayer in

00:05:49.805 --> 00:05:56.045
his Battle Drone's demo. Anthropic released all 211 tested scorpion talks and binder designs,

00:05:56.445 --> 00:06:01.385
plus the corresponding lab data. The public resource for scientists is on hugging face.

00:06:01.385 --> 00:06:07.896
An independent Schlottski's and Sinabon franchisee used chat GPT work to cut menu repricing

00:06:07.896 --> 00:06:09.756
time by 95%.

00:06:10.016 --> 00:06:13.116
Cash reconciliation dropped to 94% less time.

00:06:13.696 --> 00:06:19.256
The open AI blog says the work surfaced a workflow that could free roughly $100,000 in cash

00:06:19.256 --> 00:06:19.556
flow.

