00:06:54.491 --> 00:07:01.111
IBM Research released ALTK Evolve on the Hugging Face blog, using learned memory to reach

00:07:01.111 --> 00:07:05.971
the top of the Tao-squared Bench customer service leaderboard without requiring a frontier

00:07:05.971 --> 00:07:06.431
model.

00:07:07.424 --> 00:07:11.964
Paste Simon Willison's proofreading prompt into your editor and run it on the next technical

00:07:11.964 --> 00:07:12.884
document you write.

00:07:13.404 --> 00:07:16.464
It catches subtle phrasing issues that generic prompts miss.

00:07:17.224 --> 00:07:22.864
Run Mopey Laura on an Accented English ASR fine-tune when you do not want a separate module

00:07:22.864 --> 00:07:23.564
per accent.

00:07:23.564 --> 00:07:29.104
Try the Learned Readout Token Confidence Probe on your current generation pipeline as a

00:07:29.104 --> 00:07:30.264
one-line insertion.

00:07:30.864 --> 00:07:36.684
Evaluate Lamb Style Layton Multi-Hypothesis Memory on any long horizon agent task, where

00:07:36.684 --> 00:07:40.224
competing explanations must be retained without bloating the context.

00:07:41.202 --> 00:07:46.402
More labs are likely to publish non-English chain-of-thought inspection tools following Carpathi's

00:07:46.402 --> 00:07:46.982
observation.

00:07:47.782 --> 00:07:52.762
Additional low resource web agent benchmarks and adaptation recipes are anticipated after

00:07:52.762 --> 00:07:58.684
the low agent release. Shared prompts shrink per task traces, and that is the failure we

00:07:58.684 --> 00:08:03.784
pop the hood on for implicit budgeting under task composition. When several tasks share

00:08:03.784 --> 00:08:08.744
a single prompt, models allocate fewer tokens to each task than they would in isolation.

00:08:09.504 --> 00:08:14.824
That happens even when the total context remains comfortably inside the window. The model maintains

00:08:14.824 --> 00:08:20.724
an implicit per task compute budget that shrinks under competition. Tasks whose isolated solutions

00:08:20.724 --> 00:08:24.344
versions already require long traces to suffer the largest accuracy drop.

00:08:24.744 --> 00:08:27.784
The budgeting is visible in token counts per subtask.

00:08:28.304 --> 00:08:33.344
Errors rise suddenly once any single task's trace length exceeds a model-specific threshold.

00:08:33.984 --> 00:08:38.844
Adding explicit per-task length instructions or forcing intermediate verification steps

00:08:38.844 --> 00:08:43.664
restores most of the loss performance at the cost of extra tokens overall.

00:08:44.344 --> 00:08:49.084
Measure per-task token usage on representative multitask prompts before deployment.

00:08:49.084 --> 00:08:54.924
If any task routinely exceeds roughly 60% of its isolated length, split the prompt

00:08:54.924 --> 00:08:58.644
or add verification rather than relying on the model to self-regulate.

